a second missile field capable of  housing nuclear missiles that could  reach the u.s  has just been discovered in china lucas  tomlinson at the pentagon shows us the  evidence and gets official reaction  to that discovery tonight for the second  time in two months  new satellite photos show china building  over a hundred silos to house nuclear  missiles  when complete it will have more than two  hundred that's half the number of  land-based silos the u.s military has  in the western united states silos are  great for  is soaking up enemy warheads  if you look at china's silos which now  are on the kind of order of 240  it takes at least two nuclear warheads  to destroy each silo  jeffrey lewis an expert on china's  nuclear arsenal is part of a team that  discovered the first missile site in  june  he says when operational chinese  missiles carrying multiple nuclear  warheads  can reach targets over 9 000 miles away  putting all of the united states in  range  the head of u.s forces in the pacific is  also sounding the alarm  china is coming at us rapidly  that includes economically  diplomatically and militarily  the state department also taking note of  china's rapidly growing nuclear arsenal  quote  beijing has sharply deviated from its  decades-old nuclear strategy  based on minimum deterrence in its  annual report to congress on china the  pentagon warned  over the next decade china's nuclear  warhead stockpile  currently estimated to be in the low  200s is projected to at least  double in size as china expands and  modernizes  its nuclear forces the u.s has more than  5 000 nuclear warheads  china and the united states have no  nuclear arms control treaties  i think very important that we find a  way  to at least talk about how we want to  manage this hostility  so that you know we don't end up in a  nuclear war  early next month the pentagon is  expected to release its new annual  report  detailing china's military expansion  including its nukes  brett lucas 